PROJECT-SPECIFIC REVIEW NOTES
- This project spans two independent TypeScript codelines: mocka (fare rules, src/fares.ts) and mockb (departure board, src/schedule.ts). Each has its own tsconfig.json and package.json; there is no shared root.
- Both codelines use TypeScript strict mode ("strict": true, ES2022 modules, bundler resolution). The type-check command is `tsc --noEmit` (npm run build). Tests run via `vitest run` (npm test). No linter is configured.
- Source files live under src/; tests live under test/ and import via relative paths (e.g. ../src/fares). Tests use vitest's describe/it/expect idioms.
- The expected fixes are minimal one-line logic changes. Flag any diff that touches more than the single offending comparison or loop bound, or that introduces new files, dependencies, or exports.
- Bug class to scrutinise — boundary / off-by-one: MOCK3-1 concerns an inclusive boundary (age >= 65 vs the current strict > 65); MOCK3-2 concerns a loop bound (i < stops.length - 1 drops the final stop). Confirm the fix makes the boundary inclusive (or the loop iterates the full length) and that existing tests still pass.
- Test coverage gaps to check: the current test suites do not exercise the exact boundary (age 65 for fares; final stop appearing in formatStops output for schedule). A correct implementation should add or already include a test that covers the previously failing case. If no such test was added, note it as a major issue.
- Do not run build or test commands yourself; rely on the diff and the acceptance criteria. Assess whether the change would pass `tsc --noEmit` and `vitest run` by inspection.

